  "conclusion": "Ordinary Windows native-speaker start/stop sends no hidden qcadcm codec-register hardware-resource payload: every marked 0x2004 request is core, clock, or endpoint GPIO. Denali/Hamoa Linux also maps COMP to the same left/right master ports and Windows timing/offsets, and the SoundWire core allocates all four channels from ch_mask=0x0f. The remaining DRE/CSR parity gap is therefore inside WSA-macro COMP producer/runtime semantics or another downstream dependency, not an omitted host resource table or DP2 lane/mask allocation error."
